  "topic": "hover",
  "subtopic": "deduced_types",
  "title": "Generic lambda parameters",
  "summary": "A generic lambda's `auto` parameter is the type the lambda is called with, and the parameter's members have cards",
  "prose": "Inside the body the parameter reads as the type of the call, and `point.x`\nis the member of that type. A lambda called with several types keeps its\nparameter `auto`.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [
    "clangd#493",
    "clangd#1768"
  ],
